  "body": "This bug is motivated by https://crbug.com/952834 where Chromium's implementation of the Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy has incorrectly applied to downloads triggered by Save-Link-As context menu.  IMO such downloads should be considered browser-initiated (since triggering them requires going through trusted browser UI [the context menu]).\r\n\r\nSuch download requests use [mode](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-mode) set to `no-cors` which makes them subject to CORP (FWIW, I don't think `navigate` mode should be used for downloads and I don't see a separate mode just for downloads).\r\n\r\nI note that the concept of \"browser-initiated\" requests is not well defined in specs today (I think).  See also \"[Directly User-Initiated Requests](https://mikewest.github.io/sec-metadata/#directly-user-initiated)\" discussed for [`Sec-Fetch-Site: none`](https://mikewest.github.io/sec-metadata/#sec-fetch-site-header)\r\n\r\n/cc @mikewest @annevk @youennf @johnwilander @csreis",
